## Scenario 1: Delayed Uplink — Bundle Storage Demonstration
##
## TCP terrestrial peer delivers bundles immediately.
## LTP contact to satellite (node 20) does not open until +30 seconds.
## Bundles queue in ION's bundle storage until the contact window opens,
## then burst out over LTP.
##
## This demonstrates DTN store-and-forward behavior.

1 10 ''
s

# Self-contact (always available)
a contact +0 +86400 10 10 100000000

# Terrestrial link (node 30) — available immediately
a contact +0 +86400 10 30 100000000
a contact +0 +86400 30 10 100000000

# Satellite link (node 20) — DELAYED: opens at +30s
a contact +30 +86400 10 20 9600
a contact +30 +86400 20 10 9600

# Ranges
a range +0 +86400 10 10 0
a range +0 +86400 10 20 1
a range +0 +86400 20 10 1
a range +0 +86400 10 30 0
a range +0 +86400 30 10 0
